  "notes": [
    "Sawn timber (mitcad#478): Mitcad's own parts of industry-standard sizes, no supplier. Sizes are thickness x width in mm, nominal at 20 % moisture; the less common sizes are rows marked availability 'less common'. Re-sawn sizes are 2 mm narrower than nominal.",
    "Species: pine for thicknesses 19 and 25, spruce for the others (22 and 44 usually spruce).",
    "Densities at 20 % moisture: spruce 450 kg/m3, pine 520 kg/m3. Grounds: the mean density of strength class C24 (EN 338) is 420 kg/m3 at 12 % moisture, and the usual mean of spruce is 430-450 kg/m3 and of pine 480-500 kg/m3 there; a piece at 20 % moisture is about (1 + 0.20) / (1 + 0.12) = 1.07 times as heavy for nearly the same volume, so 450 and 520 (rounded). Checked against no supplier's data; good to within some 10 %.",
    "Tolerances (sawn): up to 100 mm -1/+3 mm, over 100 mm -2/+4 mm, for thickness and width each."
  ],
